# Supabase — both of these are PUBLIC by design and ship inside the browser
# bundle. Anything prefixed VITE_ is readable by anyone who opens the site.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Everything above is PUBLIC. Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the
# JavaScript that every visitor downloads — that is how the browser reaches
# Supabase at all, and both values above are designed for it. Security comes
# from row level security and column privileges, not from hiding these.
#
# Secrets go below, WITHOUT a VITE_ prefix, and never reach the browser:
#
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...     bypasses all RLS; ops scripts only
#
# `npm run check:bundle` fails the build if any non-VITE_ value appears in
# dist/, which is what stops a mis-prefixed secret from shipping.

# --- Edge function secrets (supabase/functions/whatsapp-webhook) ------------
# These never live in .env and are never read by the site build. They are set
# on the Supabase project itself, from .env.functions (also gitignored):
#
#   npx supabase secrets set --env-file .env.functions --project-ref <ref>
#
#   WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=   the string also pasted into Meta's "Verify token"
#   WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=     Meta > App settings > Basic > App secret
#
# A secret name may not begin with SUPABASE_ — Supabase reserves that prefix.
